Q: NLog 6.0.7 Multiple archives created in multi-process logging setup A: <p>Think this will work better for handling multiple processes concurrently writing to the same file with archive enabled:</p>
<pre class="lang-json prettyprint-override"><code>&quot;extensions&quot;: [
  {
    &quot;assembly&quot;: &quot;NLog.Extensions.Logging&quot;
  },
  {
    &quot;assembly&quot;: &quot;NLog.Targets.AtomicFile&quot;
  }
],
&quot;targets&quot;: {
  &quot;async&quot;: true,
  &quot;fileLog&quot;: {
    &quot;type&quot;: &quot;AtomFile&quot;,
    &quot;layout&quot;: &quot;${verbose}&quot;,
    &quot;fileName&quot;: &quot;${basedir}/logs/App_${shortdate}.log&quot;,
    &quot;archiveAboveSize&quot;: &quot;104857600&quot;,
    &quot;maxArchiveDays&quot;: &quot;14&quot;
  }
}
</code></pre>
<p>Instead of using old style <code>File.Move</code> with static <code>App.log</code>-filename, then it will roll to the next filename using <code>${shortdate}</code>.</p>
<p>The new archive-logic:</p>
<ul>
<li>App_20251230.log (Oldest file)</li>
<li>App_20251230_01.log</li>
<li>App_20251230_02.log (Newest file)</li>
</ul>
<p>The old static archive-logic:</p>
<ul>
<li>App.log (Newest file)</li>
<li>App_20251230_01.log (Oldest file)</li>
<li>App_20251230_02.log</li>
</ul>
<p>See also <a href="https://nlog-project.org/2025/04/29/nlog-6-0-major-changes.html" rel="nofollow noreferrer">NLog v6 - FileTarget and ArchiveSuffixFormat</a></p>

Q: .net - How to change exception message of Exception object? A: 
<p>You can change the exception message via reflection like this...</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>Exception exception = new Exception(&quot;Some message.&quot;);
var type = typeof(Exception);
var flags = BindingFlags.Instance | BindingFlags.NonPublic;
var fieldInfo = type.GetField(&quot;_message&quot;, flags);
fieldInfo.SetValue(exception, message);
</code></pre>
<p>So you can create an extension method...</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>namespace ExceptionExample
{
    public static class ExceptionExtensions
    {
        public static void SetMessage(this Exception exception, string message)
        {
            if (exception == null)
                throw new ArgumentNullException(nameof(exception));

            _fieldInfo?.SetValue(exception, message);
        }

        //cached reflection-info in a static var for performance
        private static FieldInfo _fieldInfo
            = typeof(Exception).GetField(&quot;_message&quot;, BindingFlags.Instance | BindingFlags.NonPublic);
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>And then use it...</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>...
using static ExceptionExample.ExceptionExtensions;

public class SomeClass
{
    public void SomeMethod()
    {
        var reader = AnotherClass.GetReader();
        try
        {
            reader.Read();
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            var connection = reader?.Connection;
            ex.SetMessage($&quot;The exception message was replaced.\n\nOriginal message: {ex.Message}\n\nDatabase: {connection?.Database}&quot;);
            throw; // you will not lose the stack trace
        }
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>You have to keep in mind that <strong>if you use &quot;throw ex;&quot; the stack trace will be lost</strong>.</p>
<p>To avoid this <strong>you must use &quot;throw;&quot; without the exception</strong>.</p>

Q: Codependent menu selections in Streamlit A: <p>ok, I think I got it. Finally tricked ChatGPT into giving a working answer lol</p>
<pre><code>from datetime import datetime as dt
import streamlit as st
import pandas as pd
from io import BytesIO
import uuid

st.set_page_config(layout=&quot;wide&quot;)
st.markdown(
    &quot;&lt;h1 style='text-align: center; margin-top: -4rem;'&gt;Materials Creation&lt;/h1&gt;&quot;,
    unsafe_allow_html=True
)

# -------------------------------------------------
# Session state initialization
# -------------------------------------------------
if &quot;materials_df&quot; not in st.session_state:
    st.session_state.materials_df = pd.DataFrame()

if &quot;edit_id&quot; not in st.session_state:
    st.session_state.edit_id = None

if &quot;last_edit_id&quot; not in st.session_state:
    st.session_state.last_edit_id = None

if &quot;last_category&quot; not in st.session_state:
    st.session_state.last_category = None

# -------------------------------------------------
# Load source Excel
# -------------------------------------------------
@st.cache_data
def load_data(path=&quot;Sample.xlsx&quot;):
    return pd.read_excel(path)

df = load_data(&quot;Sample.xlsx&quot;)

# -------------------------------------------------
# Menu headers
# -------------------------------------------------
menu_config_headers = {
    'Polymer': ['Manufacturer', 'Subtype', 'Product Name', 'Grade', 'Color'],
    'Coating': ['Manufacturer', 'Subtype', 'Product Name', 'Grade', 'Color'],
    'Misc': ['Manufacturer', 'Subtype', 'Product Name', 'Grade', 'Color'],
    'Solder Paste': ['Manufacturer', 'Grade', 'Flux', 'Metal Load', 'Powder Size', 'Recycled Content', 'Solder Alloy'],
    'Solder Alloy': ['Manufacturer', 'Grade', 'Form', 'Recycled Content', 'Perform Size', 'Solder Alloy'],
    'Shaped Metal': ['Manufacturer', 'Subtype', 'Product Name', 'Grade', 'Form', 'Metal/Alloy', 'Recycled Content', 'Standard and Standard Designating Body', 'Thickness'],
    'Bulk Metal': ['Manufacturer', 'Grade', 'Form', 'Metal/Alloy', 'Purity/Concentration', 'Recycled Content', 'Standard and Standard Designating Body'],
    'Plating': ['Manufacturer', 'Form', 'Manufacturer Performing Plating', 'Metal/Alloy', 'Purity/Concentration', 'Recycled Content'],
    'Chemical': ['Manufacturer', 'Chemical Name / Description', 'Purity/Concentration'],
    'Magnet': ['Manufacturer', 'Subtype', 'Grade', 'Recycled Content'],
    'Process': ['Manufacturer', 'Subtype', 'Product Name', 'Grade'],
    'Semiconductor': ['Manufacturer', 'Grade', 'Semiconductor Description', 'Semiconductor Type'],
    'Surface Treatment Process': ['Manufacturer', 'Subtype', 'Color', 'Composition of Coating / &quot;Target&quot; Material', 'Purity/Concentration', 'Substrate: Base Metal', 'Surface Treatment Type / Specification'],
    'Anodization': ['Manufacturer', 'Color', 'Anodization Details', 'Metal + &quot;Anodizing&quot;', 'Substrate: Base Metal']
}

# -------------------------------------------------
# Layout
# -------------------------------------------------
form_col, preview_col = st.columns([1, 1])

# =================================================
# FORM
# =================================================
with form_col:

    # --- Determine if we are editing a material ---
    existing_row = None
    if st.session_state.edit_id:
        existing_row = st.session_state.materials_df[
            st.session_state.materials_df[&quot;ID&quot;] == st.session_state.edit_id
        ].squeeze()

        # Only populate session state the first time we load this material
        if st.session_state.edit_id != st.session_state.last_edit_id:
            # Clear all select/input keys except Type
            for k in list(st.session_state.keys()):
                if (k.startswith(&quot;select-&quot;) or k.startswith(&quot;input-&quot;)) and k != &quot;select-Type&quot;:
                    del st.session_state[k]

            # Populate previous values
            for field, value in existing_row.items():
                if field not in [&quot;ID&quot;, &quot;Type&quot;] and pd.notna(value):
                    st.session_state[f&quot;select-{field}&quot;] = value

            # Pre-fill Type menu
            st.session_state[&quot;select-Type&quot;] = existing_row[&quot;Type&quot;]

            st.session_state.last_edit_id = st.session_state.edit_id
            st.session_state.last_category = existing_row[&quot;Type&quot;]

    # --- Type selectbox ---
    label_col, input_col = st.columns([0.35, 0.65])
    with label_col:
        st.markdown(
            &quot;&lt;div style='text-align: right; padding-right: 8px; font-weight: 600;'&gt;Type&lt;/div&gt;&quot;,
            unsafe_allow_html=True
        )

    with input_col:
        category = st.selectbox(
            &quot;&quot;,
            [&quot;&quot;] + list(menu_config_headers.keys()),
            index=0,
            key=&quot;select-Type&quot;,
            label_visibility=&quot;collapsed&quot;
        )

    # --- Detect Type change ---
    type_changed = st.session_state.edit_id and category != st.session_state.last_category

    if type_changed:
        # Clear dependent fields
        for k in list(st.session_state.keys()):
            if (k.startswith(&quot;select-&quot;) or k.startswith(&quot;input-&quot;)) and k != &quot;select-Type&quot;:
                del st.session_state[k]
        st.session_state.last_category = category

    selected_values = {}

    # --- Render dependent menus ---
    if category:
        base_df = df[df[&quot;Material&quot;] == category]

        for label in menu_config_headers[category]:

            filtered_df = base_df.copy()
            for other_label in menu_config_headers[category]:
                if other_label == label:
                    continue

                sel = st.session_state.get(f&quot;select-{other_label}&quot;)
                if sel and sel != &quot;➕ Add new&quot; and other_label in base_df.columns and sel in base_df[other_label].dropna().unique():
                    filtered_df = filtered_df[filtered_df[other_label] == sel]

            options = filtered_df[label].dropna().unique().tolist() if label in filtered_df.columns else []
            options_with_add = [&quot;&quot;, &quot;➕ Add new&quot;] + options

            # Use existing_row only if Type didn't change
            existing_value = None
            if existing_row is not None and not type_changed and label in existing_row and pd.notna(existing_row[label]):
                existing_value = existing_row[label]

            current_choice = st.session_state.get(f&quot;select-{label}&quot;)

            is_custom = existing_value is not None and existing_value not in options

            label_col, input_col = st.columns([0.35, 0.65])
            with label_col:
                st.markdown(
                    f&quot;&lt;div style='text-align: right; padding-right: 8px; font-weight: 600;'&gt;{label}&lt;/div&gt;&quot;,
                    unsafe_allow_html=True
                )

            if current_choice in options_with_add:
                default_index = options_with_add.index(current_choice)
            elif existing_value in options_with_add:
                default_index = options_with_add.index(existing_value)
            elif is_custom:
                default_index = options_with_add.index(&quot;➕ Add new&quot;)
            else:
                default_index = 0

            with input_col:
                choice = st.selectbox(
                    &quot;&quot;,
                    options_with_add,
                    index=default_index,
                    key=f&quot;select-{label}&quot;,
                    label_visibility=&quot;collapsed&quot;
                )

            if choice == &quot;➕ Add new&quot;:
                _, input_col = st.columns([0.45, 0.55])
                with input_col:
                    custom_value = st.text_input(
                        f&quot;↳ Enter new {label}&quot;,
                        value=existing_value if is_custom else &quot;&quot;,
                        key=f&quot;input-{label}&quot;
                    )
                selected_values[label] = custom_value
            else:
                selected_values[label] = choice or None

        record = {&quot;Type&quot;: category, **selected_values}

        col_left, col_update, col_cancel = st.columns([2, 1, 0.5])

        # --- Update / Create button ---
        with col_update:
            btn_label = &quot;Update Material&quot; if st.session_state.edit_id else &quot;Create Material&quot;
            if st.button(btn_label):
                if not st.session_state.edit_id:
                    # Create new material
                    record[&quot;ID&quot;] = str(uuid.uuid4())
                    st.session_state.materials_df = pd.concat(
                        [st.session_state.materials_df, pd.DataFrame([record])],
                        ignore_index=True
                    )
                else:
                    # Update existing material
                    idx = st.session_state.materials_df.index[
                        st.session_state.materials_df[&quot;ID&quot;] == st.session_state.edit_id
                    ][0]

                    # Detect Type change
                    old_type = st.session_state.materials_df.at[idx, &quot;Type&quot;]
                    type_changed = category != old_type

                    if type_changed:
                        # Clear old fields
                        old_fields = menu_config_headers.get(old_type, [])
                        for f in old_fields:
                            if f in st.session_state.materials_df.columns:
                                st.session_state.materials_df.at[idx, f] = None

                    # Write new fields
                    for label in menu_config_headers[category]:
                        st.session_state.materials_df.at[idx, label] = selected_values.get(label)

                    # Always update Type
                    st.session_state.materials_df.at[idx, &quot;Type&quot;] = category

                    # Reset edit state
                    st.session_state.edit_id = None
                    st.session_state.last_edit_id = None
                    st.session_state.last_category = None

                # Clear all menus after creation/update
                for k in list(st.session_state.keys()):
                    if k.startswith(&quot;select-&quot;) or k.startswith(&quot;input-&quot;):
                        del st.session_state[k]

                st.success(&quot;Material saved&quot;)
                st.rerun()

        # --- Cancel button ---
        if st.session_state.edit_id:
            with col_cancel:
                if st.button(&quot;Cancel&quot;):
                    st.session_state.edit_id = None
                    st.session_state.last_edit_id = None
                    st.session_state.last_category = None
                    for k in list(st.session_state.keys()):
                        if k.startswith(&quot;select-&quot;) or k.startswith(&quot;input-&quot;):
                            del st.session_state[k]
                    st.rerun()


# =================================================
# PREVIEW / EDIT / DELETE (unchanged)
# =================================================
with preview_col:
    content, spacer = st.columns([0.9, 0.05])
    with content:
        if st.session_state.materials_df.empty:
            st.info(&quot;No materials created yet.&quot;)
        else:
            delete_uid = None
            edit_uid = None

            st.markdown(
                &quot;&quot;&quot;
                &lt;style&gt;
                .material-preview {
                    margin: 0 0 4px 0;   
                    padding-left: 20px;  
                    text-indent: -10px;  
                    line-height: 1.4;    
                }
                .type-line {
                    margin: 0 0 4px 0;
                    padding: 2px 4px;
                    border-radius: 3px;
                    font-weight: bold;
                }
                @media (prefers-color-scheme: light) {
                    .type-line {
                        background-color: #c7dcff;
                    color: #000000 !important;
                    }
                }
                @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
                    .type-line {
                        background-color: #092536;
                        color: #ffffff !important;
                    }
                }
                &lt;/style&gt;
                &quot;&quot;&quot;,
                unsafe_allow_html=True
            )

            for _, row in st.session_state.materials_df.iterrows():
                uid = row[&quot;ID&quot;]

                with st.container():
                    for field, value in row.dropna().items():
                        if field != &quot;ID&quot;:
                            if field == &quot;Type&quot;:
                                st.markdown(
                                    f&quot;&lt;div class='type-line'&gt;{field}: {value}&lt;/div&gt;&quot;,
                                    unsafe_allow_html=True
                                )
                            else:
                                st.markdown(
                                    f&quot;&lt;div class='material-preview'&gt;• &lt;b&gt;{field}:&lt;/b&gt; {value}&lt;/div&gt;&quot;,
                                    unsafe_allow_html=True
                                )

                btn_col1, btn_col2, spacer = st.columns([1, 1, 5])
                with btn_col1:
                    if st.button(&quot;Edit&quot;, key=f&quot;edit-{uid}&quot;):
                        edit_uid = uid
                with btn_col2:
                    if st.button(&quot;Delete&quot;, key=f&quot;delete-{uid}&quot;):
                        delete_uid = uid

            if delete_uid:
                st.session_state.materials_df = st.session_state.materials_df[
                    st.session_state.materials_df[&quot;ID&quot;] != delete_uid
                ]

                # Reset edit state
                if st.session_state.edit_id == delete_uid:
                    st.session_state.edit_id = None
                    st.session_state.last_edit_id = None
                    st.session_state.last_category = None

                # --- Clear all menus on the left ---
                for k in list(st.session_state.keys()):
                    if k.startswith(&quot;select-&quot;) or k.startswith(&quot;input-&quot;):
                        del st.session_state[k]

                st.rerun()


            if edit_uid:
                st.session_state.edit_id = edit_uid
                st.rerun()

            st.divider()

            col_left, col_center = st.columns([0.5, 1])
            with col_center:
                output = BytesIO()
                with pd.ExcelWriter(output, engine=&quot;xlsxwriter&quot;) as writer:
                    st.session_state.materials_df.drop(columns=[&quot;ID&quot;], errors=&quot;ignore&quot;).to_excel(
                        writer, index=False, sheet_name=&quot;Materials&quot;
                    )
                timestamp = dt.now().strftime(&quot;%Y%m%d&quot;)
                st.download_button(
                    &quot;Download materials&quot;,
                    data=output.getvalue(),
                    file_name=f&quot;Materials_{timestamp}.xlsx&quot;,
                    mime=&quot;application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet&quot;
                )
</code></pre>

Q: Does a const qualifier inside a struct member declaration do anything? A: <p>In structs as elsewhere,</p>
<ul>
<li><code>const int bar</code> (aka <code>int const bar</code>) means that <code>bar</code> is a constant <code>int</code>. Once initialized, the object can't be modified directly.</li>
<li><code>int * const bar</code> means that <code>bar</code> is a constant pointer to an <code>int</code>. Once initialized, the field can't be modified directly.</li>
<li><code>const int * bar</code> (aka <code>int const * bar</code>) means that <code>bar</code> is a pointer to a constant <code>int</code> object. <code>bar</code> isn't constant and can be modified. But the pointer can't be used to modify the <code>int</code> object to which it points.</li>
<li><code>const int * const bar</code> (aka <code>int const * const bar</code>) means that <code>bar</code> is a constant pointer to a constant <code>int</code> object. In this situation, the pointer is constant, and it can't be used to modify the <code>int</code> object to which it points.</li>
</ul>
<p>(The <a href="https://c-faq.com/decl/spiral.anderson.html" rel="nofollow noreferrer">spiral rule</a> can be used to &quot;decipher&quot; the meaning of a declaration. If there's nothing that follows the name being declared, it simplifies to reading from back to front.)</p>
<p>This is easy to check!</p>
<pre class="lang-c prettyprint-override"><code>#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;

struct Foo {
    const int bar;  // `bar` is a constant `int`
};

int main( void ) {
   struct Foo foo = { 123 };
   foo.bar = 456;  // error: assignment of read-only member 'bar'
   printf( &quot;%d\n&quot;, foo.bar );
}
</code></pre>
<p>Changing to a pointer makes no difference:</p>
<pre class="lang-c prettyprint-override"><code>#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;

struct Foo {
    int * const bar;  // `bar` is a constant pointer to an `int`
};

int main( void ) {
   int i = 123;
   int j = 456;
   struct Foo foo = { &amp;i };
   foo.bar = &amp;j;        // error: assignment of read-only member 'bar'
   *( foo.bar ) = 789;  // ok
   printf( &quot;%d\n&quot;, *( foo.bar ) );
}
</code></pre>
<p>In your second snippet, it's not <code>bar</code> that's constant but <code>*bar</code>.</p>
<pre class="lang-c prettyprint-override"><code>#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;

struct Foo {
    const int * bar;  // `bar` is a pointer to a constant `int`
};

int main( void ) {
   int i = 123;
   int j = 456;
   struct Foo foo = { &amp;i };
   foo.bar = &amp;j;        // ok
   *( foo.bar ) = 789;  // error: assignment of read-only location '*foo.bar'
   printf( &quot;%d\n&quot;, *( foo.bar ) );
}
</code></pre>
<p>Finally, both the pointer and that to which it points are constant in the following snippet:</p>
<pre class="lang-c prettyprint-override"><code>#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;

struct Foo {
    const int * const bar;  // `bar` is a constant pointer to a constant `int`
};

int main( void ) {
   int i = 123;
   int j = 456;
   struct Foo foo = { &amp;i };
   foo.bar = &amp;j;        // error: assignment of read-only member 'bar'
   *( foo.bar ) = 789;  // error: assignment of read-only location '*foo.bar'
   printf( &quot;%d\n&quot;, *( foo.bar ) );
}
</code></pre>
